+class GridPatchDataset(IterableDataset):
+    """
+    Yields patches from images read from an input dataset. The patches are chosen in a contiguous grid sampling scheme
+    by a patch generator (for example :py:class:`PatchIter`), and each patch can be post-processed by a transform.
+    By default each element is a ``(patch, coordinates)`` pair, where the coordinates give the start and stop of each
+    dimension of the patch (including the channel dimension) in the original image.
+
+    For example, two single-channel 4x4 images, 2x2 patches and a per-patch intensity shift:
+
